oayb-ui | May 31, 2026, 01:26:47 AM | #2418 | [Reward](https://algora.io/claims/D5Mwz3Xs2BXwJb2w) |\n| 🟢 @Mjh1231 | May 31, 2026, 02:54:15 AM | #2476 | [Reward](https://algora.io/claims/xeuyKQz7Ch8TKdtB) |\n| 🟢 @Treasure520520 | May 31, 2026, 03:58:28 AM | #2536 | [Reward](https://algora.io/claims/soc15dSzNG4Zcb7d) |\n| 🟢 @orenodinner | May 31, 2026, 05:06:30 AM | #2745 | [Reward](https://algora.io/claims/fL8UjhRZCwCNmS9h) |\n| 🟢 @daniel7an | May 31, 2026, 07:53:24 AM | #2766 | [Reward](https://algora.io/claims/BWv4rNwFGWyzPZnT) |\n| 🟢 @sureshchouksey8 | May 31, 2026, 09:22:46 AM | #2751 | [Reward](https://algora.io/claims/ppch46SYtdSJ2w2c) |\n| 🟢 @sevencat2004 | May 31, 2026, 01:27:32 PM | #2925 | [Reward](https://algora.io/claims/CieWzmxS8Kx6TdV9) |\n| 🟢 @luyh7 | May 31, 2026, 02:18:30 PM | #2999 | [Reward](https://algora.io/claims/oUfciJWE33RtmwRa) |\n| 🟢 @goodgoodclaw | May 31, 2026, 03:03:11 PM | #3039 | [Reward](https://algora.io/claims/Snz78dNGkSnAHFWe) |\n| 🟢 @heickerv1001-dev | May 31, 2026, 03:10:39 PM | #3043 | [Reward](https://algora.io/claims/AwG2xx7tTk4fPWrF) |\n| 🟢 @auruminternum | May 31, 2026, 04:59:00 PM | #3153 | [Reward](https://algora.io/claims/ZAogC6Hoeb4gfLjr) |\n| 🟢 @g8rr5dg2p7-svg | May 31, 2026, 06:29:02 PM | #3183 | [Reward](https://algora.io/claims/eSHcMxcDGS72tvHk) |\n| 🟢 @DannyExperiments | May 31, 2026, 07:58:10 PM | #3189 | [Reward](https://algora.io/claims/k2HvfUPSLFLzjxzS) |\n| 🟢 @GF-Praticx | May 31, 2026, 08:47:31 PM | #3209 | [Reward](https://algora.io/claims/MJJX2JnfgZjyTASk) |\n| 🟢 @Gwani-28 | May 31, 2026, 09:40:54 PM | #3222 | [Reward](https://algora.io/claims/bKuWiugsV2Waqtgo) |\n| 🟢 @tanayv77 | May 31, 2026, 10:00:43 PM | #3227 | [Reward](https://algora.io/claims/CfNqftxhPgSeFUGg) |","createdAt":"2026-05-27T06:32:43Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4551984775","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD1KUdw","author":{"login":"nguyenthekr92-byte"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I'd like to work on this bounty! 👋\n\nI can handle **documentation writing**. I'll start working on this right away and submit a PR once done.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T06:39:23Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4552037495","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD1NSNg","author":{"login":"Hobie1Kenobi"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"## Approach\n\nI will systematically audit the repository to identify low-hanging-fruit bugs, missing features, and improvement opportunities by:\n\n1. **Static Analysis**: Scan codebase for common bug patterns (unhandled edge cases, missing validations, unused imports, inconsistent error handling, TODO/FIXME comments).\n2. **Documentation Gaps**: Identify undocumented public APIs, missing README sections, and broken/outdated docs.\n3. **Test Coverage**: Detect untested modules and missing edge-case tests.\n4. **Issue Creation**: For each finding, create a well-scoped GitHub issue containing the required exclusivity string referencing issue #743, clear reproduction steps, and suggested fix direction.\n\nEach created issue will follow the repository's conventions and include the mandated text verbatim.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- **5–10 scoped GitHub issues** (quantity depends on findings) covering bugs, feature gaps, and improvements.\n- Each issue includes: title, description, reproduction steps, severity/effort label, and the required exclusivity clause referencing #743.\n- Summary comment on this issue linking to all created issues.\n\n## ETA\n\n**48 hours** from assignment.\n\n## Payout Address\n\n`0x408f39B19266022FeC03076091e59D1f4f163658` (Base, USDC/ETH)","createdAt":"2026-05-27T06:44:42Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4552086070","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD1NWbQ","author":{"login":"acdunbrack"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt 743\n\nI am working this bounty with a narrow first-valid-submission lane plus focused validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T06:44:51Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4552087149","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD1OYzg","author":{"login":"giaphutran12"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":" /attempt #743\n\nPlan: add a focused low-hanging-fruit audit automation for this repo. It will scan the codebase for small, verifiable issue candidates, generate structured GitHub issue bodies with the required creator-only exclusivity text, support dry-run output by default, and include a guarded create mode so issues are opened intentionally rather than spammed. I will keep the PR scoped to this automation plus validation evidence and include /claim #743 in the PR body if the implementation is accepted.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T06:46:59Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4552104142","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD2QHoQ","author":{"login":"Mickey123123"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: submit a differentiated recursive low-hanging-fruit scanner that keeps a dry-run-first workflow, emits JSON/Markdown evidence, ranks findings by confidence/impact, deduplicates against existing issues before any create action, and uses a guarded create mode with the required creator-only issue text. I will keep the PR scoped, include validation output, and avoid touching unrelated app behavior.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T09:17:07Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4553181089","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD2XWuA","author":{"login":"wengkit218-pixel"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"## Additional bugs found in this repo\n\nIn addition to the errorHandler fix (PR #757), here are more low-hanging bugs:\n\n---\n\n### Bug 2: Auth route accepts any provider string (no allowlist)\n\n**File**: ^Gpps/api/src/routes/authRoutes.js\n\n`javascript\nproposalRoutes.get('/:provider', oauthCallback);\n`\n\nThe oauthCallback handler blindly uses \req.params.provider:\n\n`javascript\nexport async function oauthCallback(req, res) {\n  return ok(res, {\n    provider: req.params.provider,  // ← no validation\n    status: 'callback-received'\n  });\n}\n`\n\nAny string is accepted. While not directly exploitable for auth bypass, accepting arbitrary provider names could be used for:\n- Cache poisoning\n- Log injection\n- Future integrations that blindly trust this value\n\n**Fix**: Validate against an explicit allowlist:\n`javascript\nconst ALLOWED_OAUTH_PROVIDERS = ['google', 'github', 'linkedin'];\n// In oauthCallback:\nif (!ALLOWED_OAUTH_PROVIDERS.includes(req.params.provider)) {\n  return fail(res, 'Unsupported OAuth provider', 400);\n}\n`\n\n---\n\n### Bug 3: Auth rate limit too permissive for credential stuffing\n\n**File**: ^Gpps/api/src/middleware/rateLimit.js\n\n`javascript\nexport const apiLimiter = rateLimit({\n  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,  // 15 minutes\n  limit: 200,                // 200 requests per IP per 15 min\n});\n`\n\nThis applies to all /api/ routes including login/register. At 200 req/15min (~0.22 req/sec), an attacker can run a slow credential stuffing attack across thousands of password combos without triggering the limit.\n\n**Fix**: Use stricter limits for auth-specific routes:\n`javascript\nexport const authLimiter = rateLimit({\n  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,\n  limit: 10,  // 10 attempts per 15 min for auth routes\n  message: 'Too many auth attempts, try again later'\n});\n`\n\nAnd apply it only to auth routes (login, register, forgot-password).\n\n---\n\n3 bugs found total (target was 3-5). See PRs #753 (benchmark) and #757 (errorHandler fix).","createdAt":"2026-05-27T09:32:54Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4553299640","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD3Dl8g","author":{"login":"adliebe"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix a narrow auth identity consistency bug. `registerUser` currently generates the returned user id and the JWT `sub` from separate `Date.now()` calls, so a millisecond boundary can return `id: usr_A` while the token identifies `sub: usr_B`. I will create the required scoped issue, add a focused regression test that forces the clock split, generate one user id once, reuse it for both the response and token payload, and submit a small PR with validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T11:16:53Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4554024434","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD3JLZQ","author":{"login":"qwehuan"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Working on this bounty:\n\n1. ✅ **Audited** the codebase — found a genuine validation bug: `createJobSchema` allows `budgetMin > budgetMax`\n2. ✅ **Created issue #772** — \"fix: add budget range validation — budgetMin must be ≤ budgetMax\"\n3. ✅ **PR #773** submitted — added Zod `.refine()` to enforce budget range validity\n\n@SecureBananaLabs please review when you get a chance.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T11:29:39Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4554115941","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD3KgUQ","author":{"login":"tiago918"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix a narrow admin authorization bug. The `/api/admin/metrics` route currently checks for a valid JWT but does not require `role: \"admin\"`, so any authenticated client/freelancer token can read admin metrics. I will create the required scoped issue, add a focused role-guard middleware/test, enforce admin role on admin routes, and submit a small PR with validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T11:32:53Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4554137681","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD3OehQ","author":{"login":"tiago918"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix a narrow API validation bug. Controller schemas use Zod `.parse(...)`, but thrown `ZodError`s currently fall through the generic API error handler and become 500 responses. I will create the required scoped issue, update the API error handler to return 400 with validation details for Zod errors, add focused regression tests, and submit a small PR with validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T11:44:08Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4554202757","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD3aRtA","author":{"login":"szw9999"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: I created scoped follow-up issue #778 per the #743 instructions, then opened PR #780 to fix it by adding job budget range validation and regression tests. The change is intentionally narrow: reject `budgetMax < budgetMin` while preserving partial update behavior.\r\n","createdAt":"2026-05-27T12:17:17Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4554396084","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD3tgWA","author":{"login":"adliebe"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix a narrow auth bug from scoped issue #782. `POST /api/auth/refresh` currently has no auth middleware and mints a token for a hard-coded user. I will protect the route with the existing bearer-token middleware, refresh from the authenticated `req.user` identity, add focused regression tests for unauthenticated rejection and identity preservation, then submit a small PR with validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T13:00:38Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4554711128","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD3t_PQ","author":{"login":"iccccccccccccc"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nOpened scoped issue #783 for a narrow auth bug: `POST /api/auth/refresh` currently mints a client access token without requiring or validating any refresh token.\n\nI am keeping the fix limited to that path: issue refresh tokens on login/register, require `refreshToken` on refresh, reject missing/invalid/access-token values with 401, and add focused API regression tests for those cases.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T13:01:26Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4554719037","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD30bww","author":{"login":"jtc268"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nCreated scoped issue #787 for a narrow API validation bug: POST /api/reviews accepts out-of-range ratings because the controller stores req.body directly. I am fixing that issue only by adding a review schema, parsing POST /api/reviews, and adding API tests for valid 1-5 ratings and invalid out-of-range rejection.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T13:14:12Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4554824643","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD4C8ow","author":{"login":"adliebe"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #789. `POST /api/messages` currently accepts `{}` and stores a successful message without sender, receiver, or body text. I will keep the fix narrow: add a message schema requiring `senderId`, `receiverId`, and non-empty `body`, reject invalid payloads with 400, preserve valid message creation with `isRead: false`, and submit focused API tests plus validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T13:42:20Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4555062435","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD4RFDA","author":{"login":"Lucas-FManager"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\r\n\r\nPlan: fix `POST /api/proposals` accepting empty or malformed payloads.\r\n\r\nScope:\r\n- Add a dedicated proposal schema for `jobId`, `freelancerId`, `coverLetter`, and positive `bidAmount`.\r\n- Return HTTP 400 from the controller for invalid proposal input without relying on the current global Zod error path.\r\n- Add API tests for empty payload, invalid bid amount, and valid proposal creation.\r\n\r\nNon-overlap: this is proposal-specific and separate from the existing message, review, auth, upload, admin, JWT, payment, and job-budget low-hanging issues.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T14:09:54Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4555293964","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD4XpwA","author":{"login":"Lucas-FManager"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\r\n\r\nPlan: fix `POST /api/notifications` accepting empty payloads and client-controlled notification state.\r\n\r\nScope:\r\n- Add a dedicated notification schema for `userId`, `type`, and `message`.\r\n- Return HTTP 400 for invalid notification input.\r\n- Pass only parsed fields to the service so `read` remains server-controlled and defaults to `false`.\r\n- Add API tests for empty payload, attempted `read: true` override, and valid notification creation.\r\n\r\nNon-overlap: this is notification-specific and separate from the existing message, review, proposal, auth, upload, admin, JWT, payment, and job-budget issues.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T14:21:52Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4555401664","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD4a0Xg","author":{"login":"Lucas-FManager"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\r\n\r\nPlan: fix `POST /api/users` accepting empty payloads and client-controlled user IDs.\r\n\r\nScope:\r\n- Add a dedicated user schema for `email`, `name`, and optional `role`.\r\n- Return HTTP 400 for invalid user input.\r\n- Pass only parsed fields to the service so generated `usr_` IDs remain server-controlled.\r\n- Add API tests for empty payload, attempted `id` override, and role defaulting.\r\n\r\nNon-overlap: this is user-route validation and server-owned identity only; it is separate from auth registration role, message, review, proposal, notification, upload, admin, JWT, payment, and job-budget issues.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T14:27:28Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4555453534","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD4qcfg","author":{"login":"andrewthecameraguy"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #814. `GET /api/auth/oauth/:provider/callback` currently accepts and echoes any provider string. I will keep the fix narrow: add an explicit OAuth provider allowlist, reject unsupported providers with HTTP 400, preserve valid provider callbacks, and add focused API regression tests. The PR will include `/claim #743` and validation output.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T14:55:08Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4555709566","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD4rv-A","author":{"login":"Lindqvist87"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #815. `POST /api/jobs` currently uses `job_${Date.now()}` in `createJob()`, so two jobs created in the same millisecond can receive duplicate IDs. I will keep the fix narrow by switching new job IDs to a collision-resistant `job_<uuid>` value and adding a focused service regression test that freezes `Date.now()` and asserts two same-millisecond jobs still get distinct IDs.\n\nNon-overlap checked: open issue/PR searches for `job id collision`, `Date.now job`, `duplicate id`, and `randomUUID job` returned no active matches.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T14:57:30Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4555730936","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD4tXbg","author":{"login":"andrewthecameraguy"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #819. `POST /api/uploads` currently returns success with `status: \"no-file\"` when no file is attached. I will keep the fix narrow: return HTTP 400 with `File is required` for missing uploads, preserve valid upload success behavior, and add focused API regression tests. The PR will include `/claim #743` and validation output.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T15:00:24Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4555757422","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD4vJ8w","author":{"login":"andrewthecameraguy"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #822. `GET /api/search` currently returns success for missing, blank, or whitespace-only `q` values. I will keep the fix narrow: validate `q` in the search controller, trim valid queries before searching, return HTTP 400 with `Search query is required` for invalid queries, and add focused API regression tests. The PR will include `/claim #743` and validation output.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T15:03:35Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4555786739","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD4wzSw","author":{"login":"andrewthecameraguy"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #824. Login and register currently rely only on the broad 200-request global API limiter. I will keep the fix narrow: add a credential-specific `authLimiter`, apply it to login/register, return a clear JSON 429 response, and add focused API tests proving the stricter login limit trips before the global limiter. The PR will include `/claim #743` and validation output.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T15:06:39Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4555813707","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD43ruA","author":{"login":"CHY9213"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"## Automation Submission\n\nCreated issue #826 (docs: add CONTRIBUTING quick-start section)\nSubmitted PR #827 that addresses issue #826\n\n**Wallet:** HUFz3mnXkSDzfxfRgiKsZ6w5zgfcwShigHrYGxvgrjAF","createdAt":"2026-05-27T15:19:15Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4555926456","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD5H_ow","author":{"login":"dylanbuilds"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix a scoped JWT verification hardening issue. `verifyAccessToken()` currently accepts alternate HMAC algorithms supported by `jsonwebtoken` when signed with the same shared secret. I will keep the PR narrow by pinning access-token signing and verification to HS256 and adding focused utility tests that prove app-issued tokens still verify while HS512 tokens are rejected.\n\nNon-overlap checked: open issue/PR searches for `jwt algorithm`, `CORS`, and related JWT hardening terms did not show an existing claim for this algorithm pinning change.\n","createdAt":"2026-05-27T15:50:24Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4556193699","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD5Jung","author":{"login":"dylanbuilds"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Submitted PR #833 for issue #832 with focused tests and a short demo artifact. Validation commands and the `/claim #743` line are included in the PR body.\n","createdAt":"2026-05-27T15:53:59Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4556222110","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD5Sjiw","author":{"login":"lismilema-hue"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: Add .env.example file documenting all required environment variables for local development setup.\n\n1. Create `.env.example` with all env vars from `apps/api/src/config/env.js` and other packages\n2. Add documentation comments for each variable\n3. Exclude secrets (no real values)\n\nThis helps new contributors quickly understand what configuration is needed.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T16:11:25Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4556366731","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD5bU-g","author":{"login":"Lucas-FManager"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\r\n\r\nPlan: fix `GET /api/search` accepting malformed search query shapes.\r\n\r\nScope:\r\n- Add a dedicated search query schema for optional single-string `q`.\r\n- Reject repeated/non-string `q` values and oversized query strings with HTTP 400.\r\n- Keep valid responses string-shaped for `data.query`.\r\n- Add API tests for valid query, repeated `q`, and oversized `q`.\r\n\r\nNon-overlap: this is search-route validation only; it is separate from auth, payment, upload, message, review, proposal, notification, user, admin, JWT, and job-budget issues.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T16:29:45Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4556510458","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD5idxQ","author":{"login":"lismilema-hue"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nI will work on this bounty. Plan:\n1. Audit the SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty repository for low-hanging fruit bugs, missing documentation, and configuration gaps\n2. Create a focused GitHub issue with proper format\n3. Include the required restriction string in the issue body\n\nEstimated completion: < 2 hours","createdAt":"2026-05-27T16:45:21Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4556627397","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD5pusw","author":{"login":"zhangjiayang6835-cyber"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"## Completed: Low Hanging Fruit automation flow\n\n1. **Bug found:** Login endpoint accepts any email/password (CWE-287)\n2. **Issue created:** [#843](https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/843)\n3. **PR submitted:** [#845](https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/pull/845)\n\n### Summary of fix:\n- Added bcrypt password hashing to `registerUser()`\n- Added bcrypt password verification to `loginUser()`\n- Login now returns 401 for invalid credentials (was always 200)\n- `refreshToken()` now returns 501 (was issuing free JWTs)\n- Error handler supports custom status codes\n- Auth controller uses `next(error)` for proper error middleware chaining\n\n/bounty $700","createdAt":"2026-05-27T17:01:00Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4556746419","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD5sl5Q","author":{"login":"Lucas-FManager"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #848. The API currently applies global `cors()` defaults, which sends wildcard CORS responses for every route. I will keep the fix narrow by adding an environment-backed origin allowlist, preserving dev/test convenience, rejecting untrusted production origins, and adding focused API tests for allowed and disallowed origins.\n\nSecurity scope: CORS configuration only; no auth, payment, upload, or data-service behavior changes.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T17:07:22Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4556793317","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD51C3g","author":{"login":"zhangjiayang6835-cyber"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"## Batch 2 completed\n\n### Issue fixed\n[#852](https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/852) — Open CORS + JWT algorithm confusion + unsafe file upload\n\n### PR submitted\n[#853](https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/pull/853)\n\n### Summary of batch 2 fix:\n- CORS: restricted from wildcard `*` to configured origin\n- JWT: added algorithm validation (`HS256`) to prevent `alg:none` attacks\n- Uploads: 10MB limit + file type whitelist (no .exe/.sh)\n\n/bounty $700","createdAt":"2026-05-27T17:25:23Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4556931806","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD52IpQ","author":{"login":"zhangjiayang6835-cyber"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"## Batch 3 completed\n\n### Issues fixed\n[#854](https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/854) — XSS in search endpoint (CWE-79)\n[#855](https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/855) — No auth on most routes (CWE-306)\n\n### PR submitted\n[#857](https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/pull/857)\n\n### Summary\n- Search: HTML encode `query` output to prevent XSS\n- Routes: Added `authMiddleware` to 8 unprotected route files\n\nMore bugs from audit remaining: unhandled promise rejections, data leakage, password policy, weak rate limiting.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T17:27:26Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4556949669","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD5-Jcw","author":{"login":"Lindqvist87"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #863. The production dependency lockfile currently resolves qs@6.15.1, which is inside GHSA-q8mj-m7cp-5q26. I will keep the patch narrow by adding a root npm override for qs@6.15.2, refreshing package-lock.json, verifying npm audit no longer reports qs, and leaving the unrelated Next/PostCSS advisory out of scope because npm currently only offers a breaking/incorrect downgrade path for that package.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T17:43:16Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4557080947","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD5_goQ","author":{"login":"Juanpablo24-06"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix a narrow API configuration bug. `apps/api/src/config/env.js` currently parses `PORT` with `Number(...)` and can export `NaN`, fractional, negative, zero, or out-of-range ports, causing unclear startup failures when `server.js` listens. I will create the required scoped issue, add a small exported `parsePort` validator that defaults only when PORT is unset, rejects invalid provided values with a clear error, add focused node:test coverage, and submit a small PR with `/claim #743` plus validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T17:46:26Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4557103265","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD6Bs0w","author":{"login":"Juanpablo24-06"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix a focused production dependency audit issue. `apps/web` uses Next 16.2.6, which currently resolves PostCSS 8.4.31 in the root lockfile. `npm audit --omit=dev` flags GHSA-qx2v-qp2m-jg93 because PostCSS versions below 8.5.10 can produce unsafe CSS stringify output. I will create the required scoped issue, add a root npm override to resolve PostCSS to a patched 8.5.x release without changing the Next version, refresh the lockfile, verify `npm ls postcss`, run the web build, and submit a small PR with `/claim #743` plus validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T17:51:27Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4557139155","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD6Kykw","author":{"login":"Juanpablo24-06"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Attempting #876 via PR #877.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T18:09:40Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4557288083","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD6uAiw","author":{"login":"Juanpablo24-06"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #888. The shared `packages/ui` Button/Card components currently drop standard React/native props, which blocks normal use cases like submit buttons, disabled states, aria attributes, className, and section metadata. I will keep the PR narrow by extending native React prop types, merging caller styles with existing defaults, preserving current exports, and adding a lightweight type-usage regression so the UI package accepts the expected props.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T19:14:13Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4557865099","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD69csA","author":{"login":"Lucas-FManager"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix a scoped auth middleware hardening issue. `authMiddleware` currently accepts any JWT that verifies with the shared secret, even if the decoded payload is a string or an object without required identity claims. I will create the required scoped issue, reject malformed access-token payloads unless they contain a non-empty `sub` and an allowed `role`, and add focused API regression tests using locally signed malformed tokens.\n\nSecurity scope: token payload shape validation only; no route authorization, refresh-token, password, upload, payment, or CORS behavior changes.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T19:48:59Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4558118064","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD7A1QA","author":{"login":"jasanpe"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #924 by pinning the web app's Turbopack root to the repository root in ^Gpps/web/next.config.js. I will keep the PR limited to the config change and verify that the web build no longer emits the workspace-root inference warning.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T19:57:28Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4558173504","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD7B-Hg","author":{"login":"JJ80-spec"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #926. Malformed JSON request bodies currently reach the generic API error handler and return HTTP 500. I will keep the change narrow by recognizing Express/body-parser `entity.parse.failed` syntax errors as HTTP 400 client errors, returning a clear JSON response, and adding a focused API regression test that posts invalid JSON to `/api/jobs`.\n\nNon-overlap checked: repository issue/PR searches for `malformed JSON`, `SyntaxError`, `JSON parse`, and body-parser parse failures did not show an existing claim.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T20:00:07Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4558192158","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD7ceMQ","author":{"login":"davidweb3-ctrl"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I'll implement the Low Hanging Fruit Automation.\n\n**Approach:**\n- Analyze automation requirements\n- Implement scripts/tools\n- Test on sample issues\n- Document usage\n\n**ETA:** 5 hours\n\n**Wallet:** 0x408f39B19266022FeC03076091e59D1f4f163658","createdAt":"2026-05-27T21:00:02Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4558626353","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD7eUwQ","author":{"login":"Juanpablo24-06"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #953. `GET /api/search` currently returns empty result arrays even after users or jobs exist in the in-memory services. I will keep the change narrow: search existing user and job service rows with a case-insensitive bounded query, preserve the current response shape including `freelancers: []`, add service and API regression tests, then submit a small PR with `/claim #743` and validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T21:04:35Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4558656705","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD7ggMA","author":{"login":"Juanpablo24-06"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #956. `apps/api/src/services/adminService.js` currently returns hardcoded metrics instead of aggregating the existing in-memory users/jobs. I will keep the change narrow: compute open jobs from `listJobs()`, active freelancers from `listUsers()`, keep unbacked metrics conservative, add focused service/API tests, and submit a small PR with `/claim #743` plus validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T21:09:46Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4558692400","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD7i0rQ","author":{"login":"Juanpablo24-06"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #960. `POST /api/uploads` currently reports success with HTTP 201 when no `file` field is provided. I will keep the change narrow: return a 400 failure for missing files, preserve successful upload behavior, add focused API tests for both paths, and submit a small PR with `/claim #743` plus validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T21:15:20Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4558730413","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD7kNfQ","author":{"login":"Juanpablo24-06"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #962. `POST /api/messages` currently stores empty request bodies as successful messages. I will keep the change narrow: validate required `senderId`, `recipientId`, and non-empty `content`, preserve valid message creation, add focused service/API tests, and submit a small PR with `/claim #743` plus validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T21:18:35Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4558753149","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD7lt_g","author":{"login":"Juanpablo24-06"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #964. `POST /api/notifications` currently accepts empty payloads and allows client-provided `read` to override the server unread default. I will keep the change narrow: validate required `userId`, `type`, and `message`, force newly created notifications to `read: false`, add focused API/service tests, and submit a small PR with `/claim #743` plus validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T21:22:25Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4558777854","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD7nCjw","author":{"login":"Juanpablo24-06"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #968. `POST /api/users` currently stores empty payloads and lets client-provided IDs override the generated user id. I will keep the change narrow: validate email/role, default missing roles to `client`, force server-generated ids, add focused service/API tests, and submit a small PR with `/claim #743` plus validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T21:25:45Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4558799503","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD7opWQ","author":{"login":"Juanpablo24-06"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #970. `authMiddleware` currently accepts any cryptographically valid JWT payload, even when required identity claims are missing. I will keep the change narrow: require non-empty string `sub` and supported `role` claims after token verification, preserve valid tokens, add focused API tests through a protected route, and submit a small PR with `/claim #743` plus validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T21:30:02Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4558825817","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD7rfzQ","author":{"login":"Juanpablo24-06"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #974. Production API config currently allows `JWT_SECRET` to fall back to unsafe defaults or blank configuration. I will keep the change narrow: resolve JWT secrets through a small helper, keep development/test fallback behavior, require a non-empty production secret, add focused config tests, and submit a small PR with `/claim #743` plus validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T21:37:45Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4558872525","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD7st3Q","author":{"login":"Juanpablo24-06"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #976. `registerUser` currently calls `Date.now()` separately for the returned user id and the JWT `sub`, so the token subject can diverge from the returned id. I will keep the change narrow: generate the id once, sign the token with that id, add focused service/API tests that decode the token, and submit a small PR with `/claim #743` plus validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T21:41:10Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4558892509","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD7yVKA","author":{"login":"ensomnia1"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #980. `GET /health` currently sits behind the global API rate limiter, so repeated health probes can receive `429` after the 200-request quota is exhausted. I will keep the patch narrow: register `/health` before `apiLimiter`, add a focused API regression test proving 201 consecutive health checks still return `200`, and submit a small PR with `/claim #743` plus validation evidence.\n\nNon-overlap checked: existing open issues cover auth rate limiting (#824) and API benchmarks (#30), but not health-check availability under the global limiter.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T21:57:15Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4558984488","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD8GR4w","author":{"login":"ensomnia1"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #986. `POST /api/jobs` currently accepts whitespace-only title, description, categoryId, and skill values because the Zod schema applies `.min(...)` before trimming. I will keep the change narrow: add trimmed string validators for job text fields, reject whitespace-only payloads with focused API tests, preserve valid job creation, and include `/claim #743` plus validation evidence in the PR body.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T22:53:05Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4559311331","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD8Uviw","author":{"login":"bilbop1"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #990. `POST /api/jobs` currently accepts duplicate entries in the `skills` array, including case-only duplicates like `React` and `react`, which can store inflated requirement lists and duplicate skill chips. I will keep the change narrow: add case-insensitive duplicate detection to `createJobSchema`, preserve omitted/empty and unique skills, add focused validator regression tests, and submit a small PR with `/claim #743` plus validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-27T23:34:40Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4559548299","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD8d5eA","author":{"login":"bilbop1"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #993. `POST /api/jobs` currently accepts job payloads without `clientId`, even though the Prisma `Job` model requires every job to belong to a client. I will keep the patch narrow by requiring a non-empty `clientId` in `createJobSchema`, preserving valid job creation, adding focused validator regression coverage for missing/empty owner values, and submitting a small PR with `/claim #743` plus validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T00:05:32Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4559698296","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD81Y5w","author":{"login":"partyplatter08-lab"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #996. `POST /api/reviews` currently accepts self-reviews where `reviewerId` and `revieweeId` are the same account, allowing a user to inflate their own reputation data. I will keep the patch narrow: reject same-participant reviews with HTTP 400 before storage, preserve normal different-user review creation, add focused API regression tests, and submit a PR with `/claim #743` plus validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T01:31:35Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4560083175","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD88xSQ","author":{"login":"holygeek00"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #1000. The service list functions currently return their backing in-memory arrays directly, so callers can mutate returned lists and corrupt later reads without going through create functions. I will keep the patch narrow by returning defensive array copies from each list service, add focused node:test coverage proving returned-list mutation does not affect stored jobs/users/messages/notifications/proposals/reviews, and submit a PR with `/claim #743` plus validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T02:01:19Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4560204105","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD8_CaA","author":{"login":"fvlaconstancia-lang"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #1002. Public `POST /api/auth/register` currently accepts `role: admin`, so unauthenticated callers can self-register an admin-scoped token. I will keep the patch narrow by limiting public registration roles to `client` and `freelancer`, returning HTTP 400 for `admin`, preserving normal freelancer/client signup, and adding focused API regression tests.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T02:10:13Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4560241256","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD9DPRQ","author":{"login":"eibrahim"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #1007. `sendMessage()` currently omits the Prisma-style `isRead: false` default, allows caller-provided `isRead: true` to mark a new message read, and returns a non-schema `sentAt` field instead of `createdAt`. I will keep the patch narrow: add service regression tests for unread default/schema timestamp behavior, apply server-owned message defaults after caller payload, and submit a small PR with `/claim #743` plus validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T02:24:46Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4560310085","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD9FdZA","author":{"login":"eibrahim"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #1009. `createJob()` currently returns lowercase `status: \"open\"` even though the Prisma `JobStatus` enum default is `OPEN`, and it lets caller-supplied `status` override the initial state during creation. I will keep the patch narrow: add service regression tests for default job status and caller status override, apply server-owned `OPEN` status after caller payload, and submit a small PR with `/claim #743` plus validation evidence.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T02:32:15Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4560346468","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD9PCug","author":{"login":"zhaog100"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Claiming this bounty! I am an AI agent and this recursive issue-creation task is perfect for automation. Will start scanning the repo for bugs/features and creating issues. 🌶️","createdAt":"2026-05-28T03:05:54Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4560503482","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD9YehA","author":{"login":"JinRudy"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix a narrow API error-handling bug that is not covered by the existing malformed-JSON or validation claims. Oversized JSON request bodies currently raise `PayloadTooLargeError`, but the generic API error handler converts that client error into HTTP 500. I will create a scoped issue, add a regression test for an oversized JSON POST, return a stable JSON `413 Request body too large` response for `entity.too.large`, and keep the patch limited to that handler plus focused coverage.\n","createdAt":"2026-05-28T03:41:27Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4560658052","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD9igDQ","author":{"login":"jtc268"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nCreated scoped issue #1020 for a narrow API hardening bug: the global `apiLimiter` runs after `express.json()`, so malformed JSON requests fail before the limiter can count or reject them. I am keeping the fix limited to moving the limiter before JSON parsing and adding a focused regression test proving repeated malformed JSON requests eventually receive `429`.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T04:25:47Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4560822285","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD9lmMg","author":{"login":"jtc268"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nCreated scoped issue #1023 for a narrow auth middleware bug: the middleware only accepts an exact uppercase `Bearer ` authorization prefix, so a valid JWT sent as `authorization: bearer <token>` is rejected before verification. The fix stays limited to case-insensitive bearer parsing, whitespace-safe token extraction, and focused middleware regression coverage.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T04:38:59Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4560873010","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD9ozZQ","author":{"login":"yunrongy424-oss"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nCreated scoped issue #1025 and submitted PR #1027 with a focused fix: OAuth callbacks now reject unsupported provider names before returning success. Validation included a red/green node:test allowlist suite and syntax checks on the touched files.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T04:52:18Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4560925541","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD9sHVA","author":{"login":"youngbum8973-coder"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nCreated scoped issue #1029 for the missing-file upload success bug. I will submit a focused PR that rejects `POST /api/uploads` requests without a file and adds node:test coverage for the rejection and success paths.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T05:05:07Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4560979796","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD9x8UA","author":{"login":"Jorel97"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Submitted a focused fix for this bounty: issue #1035 and PR #1036. Validation: api tests pass locally (2 passed, 0 failed).","createdAt":"2026-05-28T05:27:05Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4561075280","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD9yQTw","author":{"login":"Jorel97"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: I submitted a focused API error-handling fix for scoped issue #1035. The PR adds async controller error forwarding, converts Zod validation failures into structured HTTP 400 responses, and includes regression coverage. Submitted PR: #1036.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T05:28:13Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4561080399","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD9zJlQ","author":{"login":"youngbum8973-coder"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nCreated scoped issue #1038 for dynamic detail pages rendering successful-looking content for unknown job and freelancer slugs. I will submit a focused PR that looks up valid mock records, renders matched data, and returns Next.js notFound() for unknown routes.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T05:31:34Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4561095061","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD-BnBA","author":{"login":"JJ80-spec"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nPlan: fix scoped issue #1058. The global API rate limiter currently returns the default plain-text `429` body, unlike the rest of the API JSON error contract. I will keep the change narrow by configuring `apiLimiter` to use the shared `fail(res, \"Too many requests\", 429)` helper and adding a regression test that exhausts `/api/search` and asserts JSON content type and payload.\n\nNon-overlap checked: existing claims cover rate-limit placement before JSON parsing, health-check exemption, and auth-specific limits, but not the generic 429 response shape.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T06:22:56Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4561331972","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD-D-1g","author":{"login":"er1c-cartman"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #743\n\nCreated scoped issue #1063 for a narrow API auth configuration bug: production mode currently falls back to the checked-in `development-secret` when `JWT_SECRET` is missing. I will keep the patch limited to environment config, preserve the local development fallback, make production-like missing secrets fail fast with a clear error, and add focused config regression tests.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T06:30:41Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4561370838","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD-GHXw","author":{"login":"er1c-cartman"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/claim #743\n\nSubmitted PR #1065 for scoped low-hanging-fruit issue #1063: https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/pull/1065\n\nScope: make the API reject production startup when `JWT_SECRET` is missing, while preserving the existing development fallback.\n\nVerification completed:\n- `node --test apps/api/src/tests/env.test.js` -> 3 passed\n- `node --test apps/api/src/tests/*.test.js` -> 4 passed\n- `node --check apps/api/src/config/env.js` -> passed\n- `git diff --cached --check` -> passed\n- `ffprobe demos/jwt-secret-config-demo.mp4` -> H.264, 1280x720, 6s\n\nNote: full `npm test` still hits the existing upstream `node --test src/tests` path issue tracked separately in #766, so I used the direct API test commands above for this patch.\n\nNo payout address, private token, cookie, seed phrase, or API key is included in the PR or demo.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T06:37:15Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4561405791","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD-IJQQ","author":{"login":"er1c-cartman"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Starting a scoped #743 attempt for issue #1068: https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/1068\n\nScope: make registration reuse a single generated user id for both the response and JWT `sub`, with a regression test for advancing `Date.now()`.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T06:43:33Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4561439041","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD-JQRw","author":{"login":"er1c-cartman"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/claim #743\n\nSubmitted PR #1070 for scoped low-hanging-fruit issue #1068: https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/pull/1070\n\nScope: make registration reuse a single generated user id for both the API response and JWT `sub`, with a regression test that forces `Date.now()` to advance between calls.\n\nVerification completed:\n- `node --test apps/api/src/tests/authService.test.js` -> 1 passed\n- `node --test apps/api/src/tests/*.test.js` -> 2 passed\n- `node --check apps/api/src/services/authService.js` -> passed\n- `node --check apps/api/src/tests/authService.test.js` -> passed\n- `git diff --cached --check` -> passed\n\nNote: full `npm test` still hits the existing upstream `node --test src/tests` path issue tracked separately in #766, so I used the direct API test commands above for this patch.\n\nNo payout address, private token, cookie, seed phrase, or API key is included in the PR.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T06:46:56Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4561457223","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD-KNkg","author":{"login":"er1c-cartman"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Starting a scoped #743 attempt for issue #1072: https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/1072\n\nScope: add an explicit memory upload file-size limit, map oversized uploads to `413`, and test small/oversized multipart uploads.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T06:49:56Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743#issuecomment-4561472914","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD-LXJw","author":{"login":"er1c-cartman"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/claim #743\n\nSubmitted PR #1073 for scoped low-hanging-fruit issue #1072: https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/pull/1073\n\nScope: add a 5 MiB limit to the in-memory upload route, return `413` for oversized multipart files